AgentLink Lagos - Portfolio 3 transaction & concurrency evidence
PostgreSQL: 16.16 (Ubuntu 16.16-1.pgdg24.04+1) | default isolation: read committed | deadlock_timeout: 1s

==============================================================================
D1  COMMIT - successful cash-out
     Debit customer, credit agent, credit fee wallet, insert txn + 3 ledger rows: all or nothing.
==============================================================================
  [t+ 0.011s] before    balances -> Ada N50,000.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00
  [t+ 0.060s] A         cash_out(N10,000) for Ada returned txn_id=1309722; fee = N300.00
  [t+ 0.061s] A           ledger D wallet 83004 N10,300.00
  [t+ 0.061s] A           ledger C wallet 83003 N10,000.00
  [t+ 0.061s] A           ledger C wallet 1 N300.00
  [t+ 0.062s] A         COMMIT (deferred double-entry trigger passed)
  [t+ 0.071s] after     balances -> Ada N39,700.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N310,000.00
  [t+ 0.081s] CHECK     wallets whose balance disagrees with the ledger: 0

==============================================================================
D2  ROLLBACK - failed business rule and explicit rollback
     An exception anywhere in the transaction undoes every change made before it.
==============================================================================
  [t+ 0.006s] before    balances -> Ada N50,000.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00
  [t+ 0.021s] A         ERROR: Insufficient funds: balance 20000.00, needed 25375.00
  [t+ 0.023s] A         ROLLBACK
  [t+ 0.023s] A         BEGIN; cash_out(N5,000) for Ada ... customer cancels at the POS
  [t+ 0.031s] A         inside txn Ada's balance is N44,800.00
  [t+ 0.031s] A         ROLLBACK (explicit)
  [t+ 0.179s] CHECK     transactions with ref XD2*: 0 (nothing persisted)
  [t+ 0.186s] after     balances -> Ada N50,000.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00

==============================================================================
D3  SAVEPOINT - partial rollback in a batch
     Ada pays 3 bills in one transaction; the 2nd overdraws, only it is undone.
==============================================================================
  [t+ 0.014s] before    balances -> Ada N50,000.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00
  [t+ 0.030s] A         bill 1: N15,000 debited
  [t+ 0.031s] A         bill 2: N60,000 rejected (wallet_no_overdraft) -> ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT
  [t+ 0.032s] A         bill 3: N8,000 debited
  [t+ 0.032s] A         (demo rolled back - bill payments here were not posted to the ledger)
  [t+ 0.032s] A         result inside txn was: 50,000 - 15,000 - 8,000 = 27,000; bill 2 skipped

==============================================================================
D4  ATOMICITY on crash - POS terminal loses its connection mid-transaction
     The server rolls back an uncommitted transaction when its session dies.
==============================================================================
  [t+ 0.007s] before    balances -> Ada N50,000.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00
  [t+ 0.023s] A         cash_out(N20,000) done but NOT committed (backend pid 20675)
  [t+ 0.028s] ADMIN     pg_terminate_backend(20675)  -- simulates network drop / crash
  [t+ 0.030s] A         COMMIT failed: terminating connection due to administrator command
  [t+ 0.035s] after     balances -> Ada N50,000.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00
  [t+ 0.042s] CHECK     wallets whose balance disagrees with the ledger: 0

==============================================================================
D5  LOST UPDATE - naive read-modify-write (READ COMMITTED)
     Two tellers withdraw from Ada at the same moment: A=N10,000, B=N5,000.
==============================================================================
  [t+ 0.008s] before    balances -> Ada N50,000.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00
  [t+ 0.018s] A         read balance N50,000.00 (version 0)
  [t+ 0.020s] B         read balance N50,000.00 (version 0)
  [t+ 0.021s] A         write balance = N50,000.00 - N10,000 = N40,000.00
  [t+ 0.023s] A         COMMIT
  [t+ 0.024s] B         write balance = N50,000.00 - N5,000 = N45,000.00
  [t+ 0.026s] B         COMMIT
  [t+ 0.034s] after     balances -> Ada N45,000.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00
  [t+ 0.038s] CHECK     expected 50,000 - 10,000 - 5,000 = N35,000; got N45,000.00 -> WRONG - an update was LOST

==============================================================================
D6  FIX 1 - pessimistic locking with SELECT ... FOR UPDATE
     B's read blocks until A commits, then B sees A's result.
==============================================================================
  [t+ 0.006s] before    balances -> Ada N50,000.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00
  [t+ 0.019s] A         read balance N50,000.00 (version 0)
  [t+ 1.521s] A         write balance = N50,000.00 - N10,000 = N40,000.00
  [t+ 1.522s] A         COMMIT
  [t+ 1.522s] B         read balance N40,000.00 (version 1)  [waited 1.50s for row lock]
  [t+ 1.523s] B         write balance = N40,000.00 - N5,000 = N35,000.00
  [t+ 1.524s] B         COMMIT
  [t+ 1.533s] after     balances -> Ada N35,000.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00
  [t+ 1.540s] CHECK     expected 50,000 - 10,000 - 5,000 = N35,000; got N35,000.00 -> CORRECT

==============================================================================
D7  FIX 2 - REPEATABLE READ detects the conflict
     B's UPDATE fails with SQLSTATE 40001; the application retries.
==============================================================================
  [t+ 0.007s] before    balances -> Ada N50,000.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00
  [t+ 0.022s] A         read balance N50,000.00 (version 0)
  [t+ 0.024s] B         read balance N50,000.00 (version 0)
  [t+ 0.025s] A         write balance = N50,000.00 - N10,000 = N40,000.00
  [t+ 0.025s] A         COMMIT
  [t+ 0.029s] B         ERROR 40001: could not serialize access due to concurrent update -> ROLLBACK
  [t+ 0.029s] B         retrying transaction from the start
  [t+ 0.029s] B         read balance N40,000.00 (version 1)
  [t+ 0.030s] B         write balance = N40,000.00 - N5,000 = N35,000.00
  [t+ 0.031s] B         COMMIT
  [t+ 0.039s] after     balances -> Ada N35,000.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00
  [t+ 0.043s] CHECK     expected 50,000 - 10,000 - 5,000 = N35,000; got N35,000.00 -> CORRECT

==============================================================================
D8  FIX 3 - optimistic locking with a version column
     UPDATE ... WHERE version = <version read>; 0 rows means someone else won.
==============================================================================
  [t+ 0.014s] before    balances -> Ada N50,000.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00
  [t+ 0.026s] A         read balance N50,000.00 (version 0)
  [t+ 0.028s] B         read balance N50,000.00 (version 0)
  [t+ 0.029s] A         write balance = N50,000.00 - N10,000 = N40,000.00
  [t+ 0.030s] A         COMMIT
  [t+ 0.031s] B         UPDATE ... WHERE version = old matched 0 rows -> conflict, ROLLBACK and retry
  [t+ 0.031s] B         retrying transaction from the start
  [t+ 0.031s] B         read balance N40,000.00 (version 1)
  [t+ 0.032s] B         write balance = N40,000.00 - N5,000 = N35,000.00
  [t+ 0.033s] B         COMMIT
  [t+ 0.040s] after     balances -> Ada N35,000.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00
  [t+ 0.046s] CHECK     expected 50,000 - 10,000 - 5,000 = N35,000; got N35,000.00 -> CORRECT

==============================================================================
D9  NON-REPEATABLE READ - READ COMMITTED vs REPEATABLE READ
     A (an auditor) reads Ada's balance twice while B commits a withdrawal in between.
==============================================================================
  [t+ 0.873s] A         [READ COMMITTED] first read  N50,000.00
  [t+ 0.879s] B         withdraws N7,000 and COMMITs
  [t+ 0.880s] A         [READ COMMITTED] second read N43,000.00  -> NON-REPEATABLE READ (value changed inside one transaction)
  [t+ 1.217s] A         [REPEATABLE READ] first read  N50,000.00
  [t+ 1.224s] B         withdraws N7,000 and COMMITs
  [t+ 1.224s] A         [REPEATABLE READ] second read N50,000.00  -> same snapshot, repeatable

==============================================================================
D10  WRITE SKEW / PHANTOM - agent daily cash-out limit (N100,000)
     Each session checks 'used today + amount <= limit' then inserts. Neither sees the other's insert.
==============================================================================
  --- isolation level: REPEATABLE READ
  [t+ 0.346s] A         used today N0.00; wants N60,000 -> 60,000 <= 100,000 OK
  [t+ 0.353s] B         used today N0.00; wants N70,000 -> 70,000 <= 100,000 OK
  [t+ 0.357s] A         INSERT cash-out N60,000
  [t+ 0.360s] B         INSERT cash-out N70,000
  [t+ 0.362s] A         COMMIT ok
  [t+ 0.363s] B         COMMIT ok
  [t+ 0.369s] CHECK     agent's cash-outs today = N130,000.00 -> LIMIT BROKEN (write skew)
  --- isolation level: SERIALIZABLE
  [t+ 0.714s] A         used today N0.00; wants N60,000 -> 60,000 <= 100,000 OK
  [t+ 0.718s] B         used today N0.00; wants N70,000 -> 70,000 <= 100,000 OK
  [t+ 0.720s] A         INSERT cash-out N60,000
  [t+ 0.722s] B         INSERT cash-out N70,000
  [t+ 0.724s] A         COMMIT ok
  [t+ 0.724s] B         COMMIT failed 40001: could not serialize access due to read/write dependencies among transactions
  [t+ 0.724s] B           detail: Reason code: Canceled on identification as a pivot, during commit attempt.
  [t+ 0.731s] CHECK     agent's cash-outs today = N60,000.00 -> limit respected
  Note: the production cash_out() function avoids this at READ COMMITTED by locking the
  agent's wallet row FOR UPDATE before the check, which serialises cash-outs per agent.
  [t+ 1.058s] A         cash_out(N30,000) via function, not yet committed (holds agent wallet lock)
  [t+ 1.058s] B         cash_out(N75,000) at the same agent starts...
  [t+ 2.059s] B         ... is blocked waiting for the agent-wallet row lock
  [t+ 2.062s] A         COMMIT
  [t+ 2.063s] B         rejected: Agent AGL-DEMO01 daily cash-out limit exceeded (used 30000.00, limit 100000.00)

==============================================================================
D11  DEADLOCK - transfers in opposite directions
     A: Ada -> Bayo, B: Bayo -> Ada. Unordered locking can deadlock; ordered locking cannot.
==============================================================================
  --- locking strategy: UNORDERED (source first)
  [t+ 0.436s] A         wallet_transfer(Ada 83004 -> Bayo 83005, N1,000)
  [t+ 0.436s] B         wallet_transfer(Bayo 83005 -> Ada 83004, N1,000)
  [t+ 1.943s] B         ERROR 40P01 deadlock detected -> this txn was chosen as victim, ROLLBACK
  [t+ 2.848s] A         transfer COMMITTED
  [t+ 2.858s] after     balances -> Ada N49,000.00 | Bayo N21,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00
  --- locking strategy: ORDERED (lowest wallet_id first)
  [t+ 3.203s] A         wallet_transfer(Ada 83004 -> Bayo 83005, N1,000)
  [t+ 3.203s] B         wallet_transfer(Bayo 83005 -> Ada 83004, N1,000)
  [t+ 3.216s] A         transfer COMMITTED
  [t+ 3.220s] B         transfer COMMITTED
  [t+ 3.228s] after     balances -> Ada N50,000.00 | Bayo N20,000.00 | Agent N300,000.00

